# Claude Code's local permission allowlist. Machine-specific and not shareable:
# it accumulates absolute paths that embed the local username and directory
# layout, so it has no meaning in another checkout and should not be published.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Pre-redesign stylesheet, kept on disk as a local safety net during the
# overhaul. Git is the place for old versions of a file.
.claude/styles.cozy.css.bak

# The screenshot/probe harness (shot.ps1, dump.ps1, crop.ps1, zoom.ps1,
# sync.ps1 and the sprout_preview mirror) deliberately lives in %TEMP% rather
# than in the repo, so there is nothing to ignore for it here. Noted because
# its absence is a decision, not an oversight.

# The app has no dependencies and never needs an install step. This entry is
# here for the one case that does create the directory: reaching for a
# throwaway `npx serve` in a cloud session. Nothing the app ships ever reads
# from it, so it must never reach a commit.
node_modules/

# The store wrapper's generated output. native/www is a copy of the whole app
# made by native/copy-web.js on every build, so committing it would put a
# second copy of Sprout in the repo.
native/www/
native/.capacitor/

# native/ios and native/android are deliberately NOT ignored. Capacitor can
# regenerate them, but not everything in them: the Android notification icon,
# the app icons, the signing config and any Info.plist entry are hand-made and
# live nowhere else. Ignoring them meant the first `cap add` on another machine
# silently threw all of that away. Each platform directory carries its own
# .gitignore from the Capacitor template, and those already cover the parts
# that really are generated — build output, Pods, DerivedData, the copied web
# assets and the generated capacitor.config.json.

# OS and editor cruft
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
